### Must-not-have scans

Command:
```
grep -nE 'device\.NewDevice|conn\.NewDefaultBind|tap\.CreateDummyTAP|startUAPI\(|UAPI' \
  /home/kexi/eg-super-http/integration/main_super.go \
  /home/kexi/eg-super-http/integration/main_httpserver.go \
  /home/kexi/eg-super-http/integration/main.go
```
Result: `Super` ignores `useUAPI` and `bindmode`; production startup uses
`net.Listen("tcp", ...)`. The only UAPI match in `main_super.go` is the shared
`startUAPI` definition for `main_edge.go`, not a Super call. No Super Device,
bind, TAP, or UAPI construction was found.

```
grep -RInE 'net\.(ListenUDP|DialUDP|ListenPacket)|ListenPacket\("udp|Dial\("udp' \
  /home/kexi/eg-super-http/integration --include='*.go'
```
Result: matches are pre-existing generic Edge bind/TAP code and vendored
dependencies; `device/super_stun.go` uses `device.net.bind.ParseEndpoint` and
`bind.Send`, not a socket constructor. The same-bind implementation stores the
active bind and sends STUN through it.

```
grep -RInE 'ControlPSKey.*json:|json:.*ControlPSKey' \
  /home/kexi/eg-super-http/integration --include='*.go'
```
Result: exactly two production declarations, both `json:"-"`:
`SuperConfigV2Peer.ControlPSKey` and `SuperNodeV2Ref.ControlPSKey`.

```
grep -RInE 'func edge_(get|post)_(superparams|peerinfo|nhtable|nodeinfo)|/edge/(superparams|peerinfo|nhtable|nodeinfo)' \
  /home/kexi/eg-super-http/integration --include='*.go'
```
Result: no legacy v1 `/edge/` handler/route matched.

```
  /home/kexi/eg-super-http/integration --include='*.go' --include='go.mod' --include='go.sum'
```
Result: only vendored Pion STUN URI/source comments and unrelated vendored port
names matched; no migration runtime TURN, relay, or WebSocket addition found.

Additional observation: a broad `ServerUpdate` scan still finds legacy
`ServerUpdate` parsing/dispatch in `device/receive.go` and
`device/receivesendproc.go`. It appears on the retained Edge legacy path rather
than the Super runtime; this audit does not count it as a Super UDP listener,
but it should be removed/justified before claiming the plan's stronger
"no ServerUpdate transport" wording.

