The original scans remain valid: Super starts only TCP `net.Listen` HTTP
servers, ignores UAPI/bind CLI inputs, has no Super `device.Device`, UDP bind,
dummy TAP, or UAPI construction; control PSKey JSON fields use `json:"-"`; no
legacy `/edge/` v1 handlers matched; and no project TURN/relay/WebSocket
runtime addition was found. Legacy `ServerUpdate` symbols remain in generic
Edge protocol code but are not wired to the HTTP-only Super runtime or any
Super peer path; the inspected v2 Super runtime does not construct a Device.

## Final re-review verdict

All prior rejection causes are now documented, evidenced, or pre-authorized;
the required current targeted tests pass; and main worktree preservation holds.

